# local env files
#
# Ignore every .env variant and re-admit the tracked template, rather than
# listing known suffixes. The old list covered `.env`, `.env*.local` and
# `.env-e`, so a `.env.bak` sitting next to them was committable -- and was
# committed, byte-identical to a developer's live credentials, by a stray
# `git add -A`. A deny-list only protects the suffixes someone thought of.
.env*
!.env.example

# typescript
dist/
.cache

# turbo
.turbo

# cert
*.pem
*.p12
*.p8
